                <pb facs="0698" n="690" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg690"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War, 1939/441: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Minister in Rumania</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gunther</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-09-20T20:00:00-04:00">September 20, 1939—8
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>137. Refer to Biddle’s 226, September 19, 9 p.m. Please take occasion orally and
                    informally to inquire of the Rumanian Government <pb facs="0699" n="691"
                        xml:id="pg691"/> what its attitude is toward reported German demand that it
                    refuse to allow civil officials of Polish Government to leave the country, and
                    whether reports of their internment are accurate.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
